# Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth: "Each land is a Swamp" includes Urborg itself, a Legendary Land with no land types of its own: on turn 1
# it is a Swamp and taps for {B}. A second Urborg played on turn 3 breaks the legend rule (CR 704.5j): Bot1 keeps one and the other
# goes to the graveyard, and the survivor is still a Swamp.

[Bot1 Deck]
Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth
Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth
Island x18

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth.Play
? Bot1.Battlefield.Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth.Subtypes = Swamp
Bot1.Battlefield.Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth.Activate(Ability: {B})
? Bot1.Mana = {B}
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth.Play
Bot1.Choose(Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth.Subtypes = Swamp

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 1
Bot1.Graveyard = Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth
